WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.093 --> 00:00:09.377
"You did it, Wilbur," cried Orville as his brother landed their invention.

2
00:00:09.397 --> 00:00:11.658
"Finally, we are successful.

3
00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:17.481
October the fifth of 1905 will go down in history," replied his brother.

4
00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:21.184
"Today you flew the world's first working airplane.

5
00:00:21.624 --> 00:00:23.705
You flew more than 24 miles.

6
00:00:24.245 --> 00:00:28.848
This invention is really going to change the world," exclaimed Orville.

7
00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:31.096
"And we invented it!"

8
00:00:32.537 --> 00:00:36.938
The Wright brothers were true inventors who spent their lives trying to build better machines.

9
00:00:37.678 --> 00:00:40.359
Wilbur and Orville were extremely intelligent men.

10
00:00:40.879 --> 00:00:44.020
Unlike most scientists, however, they did not go to a university.

11
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.980
They were self-taught geniuses.

12
00:00:47.381 --> 00:00:51.462
Wilbur was a fantastic student and was registered to attend Yale University.

13
00:00:51.982 --> 00:00:55.443
But in 1886 he got hit in the face with a hockey stick.

14
00:00:56.003 --> 00:00:59.244
The injury was so bad that it took him almost a year to recover.

15
00:00:59.956 --> 00:01:03.137
By the time he recovered, his mother had become very sick.

16
00:01:04.717 --> 00:01:09.279
So instead of going back to school, Wilbur spent the next year looking after his mother.

17
00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:12.280
Whenever he had a spare moment, he would read.

18
00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.021
During this time Orville also lost interest in school.

19
00:01:16.661 --> 00:01:19.162
He found a part-time job in a small printing shop.

20
00:01:21.102 --> 00:01:25.323
Orville knew that he could make a lot of money if he had a professional printing press, but

21
00:01:25.463 --> 00:01:26.984
it was far too expensive.

22
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.781
So together the two brothers built their own printing press.

23
00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:36.862
They made it almost entirely from old junk that they found themselves, including a broken tombstone.

24
00:01:39.183 --> 00:01:44.665
Soon their printing business was a success, so the brothers decided to build an even larger printing press.

25
00:01:45.325 --> 00:01:49.906
Their second press was able to print one thousand sheets an hour, which was very fast at the

26
00:01:49.966 --> 00:01:56.388
time. However, the Wright brothers were inventors and not printing men, and they soon became bored with the

27
00:01:56.428 --> 00:01:57.148
printing business.

28
00:01:58.832 --> 00:02:03.856
In 1892 the Wright brothers became interested in a new sport: bicycle riding.

29
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:09.942
Because they were excellent mechanics, they soon had their own bicycle shop and became very good at fixing

30
00:02:10.002 --> 00:02:16.427
bicycles. After a few years, Orville and Wilbur decided that they could build better bicycles than the ones

31
00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:17.027
they sold.

32
00:02:19.209 --> 00:02:22.112
So they designed two bicycles that became very popular.

33
00:02:22.812 --> 00:02:27.696
The Wright brothers were making a lot of money in the bicycle business, but making money was not

34
00:02:27.736 --> 00:02:28.717
what they liked best.

35
00:02:29.378 --> 00:02:31.279
What they loved was to learn and invent.

36
00:02:33.321 --> 00:02:39.406
During the next ten years, the Wright brothers would invent what almost everyone thought was impossible: the airplane.

37
00:02:40.086 --> 00:02:46.572
In 1896 Wilbur read a newspaper article about a famous German pilot who died flying a plane he

38
00:02:46.612 --> 00:02:47.272
had designed.

39
00:02:47.873 --> 00:02:51.336
From that moment, he became very interested in the art of flying.

40
00:02:53.084 --> 00:02:58.708
After careful thought, Wilbur and Orville guessed that the problem with the German pilot's airplane was that it

41
00:02:58.748 --> 00:02:59.829
had no controls.

42
00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.532
Of course, the Wright brothers thought they could design one that worked.

43
00:03:04.373 --> 00:03:08.756
The first thing the Wright brothers did was to read everything that they could find on aviation.

44
00:03:09.637 --> 00:03:14.941
One day while reading, Wilbur saw birds flying, and he noticed that they were constantly moving their wings

45
00:03:15.001 --> 00:03:16.482
to keep themselves balanced.

46
00:03:17.262 --> 00:03:18.924
This was the big clue that he needed.

47
00:03:21.596 --> 00:03:25.598
The Wright brothers decided to build a glider, that is, a plane with no engine.

48
00:03:26.258 --> 00:03:29.099
It had wings that moved so that they could control and turn it.

49
00:03:29.759 --> 00:03:33.301
The first two gliders that the Wright brothers built were not very successful.

50
00:03:33.801 --> 00:03:38.363
In fact, the second one was so bad that Wilbur was almost killed trying to fly it.

51
00:03:39.983 --> 00:03:45.826
After the crash, Wilbur said to his brother, "Not in a thousand years will man ever fly."

52
00:03:46.486 --> 00:03:51.128
However, after being encouraged by other engineers, they decided to try again.

53
00:03:51.856 --> 00:03:56.861
In 1902, after careful research, the Wright brothers' third glider was a success.

54
00:03:57.641 --> 00:04:00.224
Finally they had built a plane that they could control.

55
00:04:02.025 --> 00:04:05.889
The next step was to build an airplane with an engine, so that it could fly on its

56
00:04:05.949 --> 00:04:06.489
own power.

57
00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:12.534
The brothers asked many engine companies to help them build an engine and propeller for their plane, but

58
00:04:12.614 --> 00:04:13.515
no one would help them.

59
00:04:14.256 --> 00:04:18.520
So they decided to make their own engine and invented a method for making propellers.

60
00:04:19.708 --> 00:04:24.589
On December 17, 1903, the Wright brothers' first airplane was completed.

61
00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:29.951
The Flyer made four very short flights, but then crashed and was completely destroyed.

62
00:04:30.631 --> 00:04:33.752
The Wright brothers rebuilt the Flyer and called it the Flyer 2.

63
00:04:34.432 --> 00:04:36.292
It worked but had many problems.

64
00:04:37.073 --> 00:04:40.894
So in 1905, the Wrights completely rebuilt their aircraft.

65
00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.494
The Flyer 3 was amazing.

66
00:04:44.095 --> 00:04:48.676
It was the first flying machine capable of taking off and flying through the air on its own

67
00:04:48.716 --> 00:04:53.510
power. It could rise, descend, and turn in any direction that the pilot wanted.

68
00:04:54.191 --> 00:04:58.773
Wilbur flew the plane over 24 miles and landed only when his plane ran out of gas.

69
00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:02.175
It was an invention destined to change the world.
